This idea is problematic for several reasons:

1. Many people try to learn as much as they can about Nethack without
spoilers. How would some noob know to play around with jackal skin and
cuttlefish ink?
As it is, I was able to figure out that "magic markers" were used for
writing without any help.
2. This "marker equivalent" would be *much, much easier* to obtain,
skewing the game's balance. Just reverse geno cuttlefish on land and
paper golems - er, I mean, *jackals*, and voila! Scrolls aplenty!
3. Oh, then write some *more* scrolls of genocide using the resulting
materials and do the *same thing* over again, ad infinitum, or at
least until the relevant species are extinct.

Magic markers are rare for several reasons (blessed scrolls of enchant
armor, enchant weapon, and genocide are three reasons :) ), so there's
no 100% foolproof way of getting them outside of wishing. Let's keep
it that way.



